Optimize NSIS stubs, plugins, and makensis for size

The GCC-built stubs were ~116 KB where the official MSVC-built stubs
are ~38 KB, and every generated installer carries a stub. The bulk of
the difference (~65 KB) is mingw-w64's monolithic libuuid.a: pulling a
single GUID drags in every IID/PKEY constant as 20-byte .rdata$NAME
entries. Each lives in its own COMDAT-style subsection, so
-Wl,--gc-sections discards the unreferenced ones; -ffunction-sections
lets it prune unreachable code too. Add -Oz, -fno-ident, and
-fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables on top (the stubs neither throw nor
catch). Locally verified on x86: stubs drop from ~116 KB to ~50 KB and
zlib/lzma/bzip2 installers built with the patched stubs install their
payload correctly. Note -fdata-sections must NOT be added: the stubs'
custom linker script would then place zeroed buffers (.bss) into the
image, ballooning the bzip2 stub to megabytes.

Plugins link the same monolithic import libraries and get the same
treatment, except -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables: NSISdl is C++ with
exceptions, and on x86_64 (a SEH target) suppressing unwind info makes
GCC fall back to SjLj EH whose runtime our libgcc does not provide,
failing the link. makensis itself gains nothing from the earlier attempt to
append -Os at clone time, because SCons/Config/gnu appends its own -O2
afterwards and the last -O flag wins; change that -O2 to -Os directly.

--- a/SCons/Config/gnu
+++ b/SCons/Config/gnu
@@ -100,6 +100,11 @@
 stub_env.Append(CPPPATH = ['#$BUILD_CONFIG'])
 
 if not defenv['DEBUG']:
 	stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Os'])                # optimize for size
+	stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Oz'])                # prefer size over speed harder
+	stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-fno-ident'])         # drop GCC version strings
+	stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-ffunction-sections'])# one section per function
+	stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables']) # no unwind info
+	stub_env.Append(LINKFLAGS = ['-Wl,--gc-sections'])# prune unreferenced sections
 stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Wall'])                # all warnings
 stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-xc'])                  # force compile as c
@@ -126,5 +131,5 @@
 makensis_env.Append(CPPPATH = ['#$BUILD_CONFIG'])
 
 if not defenv['DEBUG']:
-	makensis_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-O2'])                # optimize
+	makensis_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Os'])                # optimize for size
 makensis_env.Append(CFLAGS = ['-Wall'])                   # all warnings
@@ -144,6 +149,10 @@
 cross_env(plugin_env)

 if not defenv['DEBUG']:
 	plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Os'])              # optimize for size
+	plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Oz'])              # prefer size over speed harder
+	plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-fno-ident'])       # drop GCC version strings
+	plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-ffunction-sections'])# one section per function
+	plugin_env.Append(LINKFLAGS = ['-Wl,--gc-sections'])# prune unreferenced sections
 plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Wall'])              # level 3 warnings
 plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-fno-strict-aliasing']) # not safe for strict aliasing
